ipts/2019/02/22/autonation-an-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2018 Q4","e":"an","d":"2019-02-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mike Jackson","x":"In January, we announced a cost-saving plan restructuring that would reduce costs by approximately $15 million annually.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/22/autonation-an-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2019 Q1","e":"an","d":"2019-04-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Cheryl Miller","x":"What we've already passed through some of the major OEM imaging cycles over the past couple of years.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/26/autonation-inc-an-q1-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2019 Q1","e":"an","d":"2019-04-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Robert Quartaro","x":"However, the first quarter 2019 results include restructuring expenses of approximately $3 million after tax or $0.03 per share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/26/autonation-inc-an-q1-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2019 Q1","e":"an","d":"2019-04-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Cheryl Miller","x":"The first quarter 2019 results include restructuring charges of approximately $3 million after tax or $0.03 per share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/26/autonation-inc-an-q1-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2019 Q2","e":"an","d":"2019-07-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Cheryl Miller","x":"On top of that, we did put in place the $50 million annualized restructuring at the beginning of the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/07/24/autonation-inc-an-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2019 Q2","e":"an","d":"2019-07-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Cheryl Miller","x":"No. We did not have restructuring costs in the second quarter, but we did have the benefit of the restructuring that we put in place rolling through in the second quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/07/24/autonation-inc-an-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2019 Q3","e":"an","d":"2019-10-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Chris Cade","x":"And then you combine that though with higher penetration rates and some pricing power that we have now in our brand extension that's been overall supportive.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/29/autonation-inc-an-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2019 Q3","e":"an","d":"2019-10-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Cheryl Scully Miller","x":"Today, we reported third quarter earnings per share from continuing operations of $1.11 per share, which included previously announced severance and related expenses of $10 million after-tax or $0.11 per share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/29/autonation-inc-an-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2019 Q3","e":"an","d":"2019-10-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Chris Cade","x":"…or $1.11 per share versus $112 million, or $1.24 per share during the third quarter of 2018, a 10% decrease on a per-share basis.EPS from continuing operations for the third quarter of 2019 included previously announced severance and related expenses of $10 million after-tax, or $0.11 per share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/29/autonation-inc-an-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2019 Q4","e":"an","d":"2020-02-11","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Cheryl Miller","x":"The warm weather is actually good for us overall with sales and we see -- we see inflation being reasonable and certainly with the tariff situation where it is we think that's in a reasonable spot.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/11/autonation-inc-an-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2019 Q4","e":"an","d":"2020-02-11","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Joe Lower","x":"Fourth quarter 2018 results included net gains from store and property divestitures of $13 million after tax, or $0.15 per share and restructuring-related charges of $7 million after tax or $0.08 per share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/11/autonation-inc-an-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2019 Q4","e":"an","d":"2020-02-11","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Joe Lower","x":"As a reminder, we incurred approximately $9 million of restructuring-related charges in the fourth quarter of 2018, which benefited the year-over-year comparison by 110 basis points.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/11/autonation-inc-an-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2020 Q1","e":"an","d":"2020-05-11","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Mike Jackson","x":"…spirit of looking at our furloughed associates standing in unemployment lines that are as far as the eye can see and not being able to get on unemployment, we did it for our associates and it was basically a pass-through from the government to try to stabilize the employment situation in America.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/11/autonation-inc-an-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2020 Q1","e":"an","d":"2020-05-11","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Joe Lower","x":"In response to dramatic sales decline during the last two weeks of March, in early April we implemented a series of cost reduction and capital preservation measures in an attempt to mitigate the economic challenges we were confronting.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/11/autonation-inc-an-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2020 Q1","e":"an","d":"2020-05-11","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mike Jackson","x":"Obviously, the wholesale market is a different story at it's very hard to judge, particularly with the auctions disrupted and with the rental car companies rightsizing their fleets.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/11/autonation-inc-an-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2020 Q2","e":"an","d":"2020-07-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mike Jackson","x":"Over the last two years, AutoNation has taken an aggressive approach to streamline the business.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/23/autonation-inc-an-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2020 Q2","e":"an","d":"2020-07-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mike Jackson","x":"Additionally in 2018, AutoNation implemented a restructuring plan that reduced cost annually, consolidated its regional structure from three to two.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/23/autonation-inc-an-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"AN 2020 Q3","e":"an","d":"2020-10-21","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"David Whiston","x":"The -- the ASP is up, but unit volume is down, and I was just curious how much of that -- that ASP increase and ultimately the increase in new vehicle gross profit is due to the higher ticket versus a mix shift to light trucks and the inventory shortage giving your pricing power.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/21/autonation-inc-an-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2020 Q3","e":"an","d":"2020-10-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Rajat Gupta","x":"Just curious as to like -- it's like all those -- this is like a good run rate to use or there is still more cost cutting measures that are in place that are fully not reflected on the SG&A side yet.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/21/autonation-inc-an-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2020 Q4","e":"an","d":"2021-02-16","l":"streaming","r":"analyst","s":"Adam Jonas","x":"I'm curious why are so many start-up EV OEMs going -- either going direct to consumer or planning to go direct to consumer, and when we put them on the spot at least saying, hey, why don't you use an AutoNation or the best of breed existing franchises to really get the leverage and time to market…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/16/autonation-inc-an-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2021 Q1","e":"an","d":"2021-04-20","l":"streaming","r":"analyst","s":"Adam Jonas","x":"So Volvo is trying to go direct-to-consumer with their EVs, right, Mike?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/20/autonation-inc-an-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2021 Q1","e":"an","d":"2021-04-20","l":"streaming","r":"analyst","s":"Adam Jonas","x":"Like what is -- just for the sake of discussion, if you're wrong, and these start-ups aren't all going down some path where they say, just kidding, we need help, we're not going to go direct-to-consumer anymore.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/20/autonation-inc-an-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2021 Q1","e":"an","d":"2021-04-20","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"David Whiston","x":"And somewhat related to that question then is, as you know, there's a balance between the amount of inventory you have and then your pricing power, and you talked about right now, you're sticking to getting the high front-end growth, which I agree with.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/20/autonation-inc-an-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2021 Q2","e":"an","d":"2021-07-19","l":"streaming","r":"analyst","s":"Michael Ward","x":"Does the digital streaming that you have and people looking online for different purchasing options, does that enhance the F&I revenue stream?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/19/autonation-inc-an-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2021 Q2","e":"an","d":"2021-07-19","l":"streaming","r":"analyst","s":"Adam Jonas","x":"Mike, I always love your opinions and wisdom around industry moves especially from OEMs, where we're seeing some auto companies looking to go direct to consumer for things like vehicle maintenance or service through OTA, and then a bit more visibly insurance and related financial services.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/19/autonation-inc-an-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2021 Q2","e":"an","d":"2021-07-19","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Mike Jackson","x":"It's not that we're raising prices on F&I, it's that the adoption rate of our products is going up and up per transaction, and every year it goes up, because we improve the products, we improve the price value for our customers and we improve our skills at presenting them to customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/19/autonation-inc-an-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2021 Q2","e":"an","d":"2021-07-19","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mike Jackson","x":"Now, so that accelerated additional cost savings.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/19/autonation-inc-an-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2021 Q2","e":"an","d":"2021-07-19","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Joe Lower","x":"So, to the point about the increase in units despite reduction in headcount.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/19/autonation-inc-an-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2021 Q3","e":"an","d":"2021-10-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mike Jackson","x":"And we modified the layout of the facility and took cost out, because we didn't see that as an opportunity.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/21/autonation-inc-an-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2021 Q4","e":"an","d":"2022-02-17","l":"streaming","r":"analyst","s":"Rick Nelson","x":"There's a view out there that the OEMs are going to start going direct to consumer, this agency model, if you will.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/02/17/autonation-an-q4-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2025 Q2","e":"an","d":"2025-07-25","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Mike Manley","x":"Clearly, there was a pull ahead of sales in late March and April in reaction to the tariff announcement, and it stands to reason that some portion of that demand was pulled ahead from the latter part of the second quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/06/autonation-an-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2025 Q2","e":"an","d":"2025-07-25","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Mike Manley","x":"Now, I know tariffs continue to be top of mind, and apart from the volume shifting I mentioned earlier, we saw limited additional impact in our Q2 results from tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/06/autonation-an-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2025 Q2","e":"an","d":"2025-07-25","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Mike Manley","x":"And I think because of that, you will see price increases in the marketplace, but very, very measured and very, very deliberate.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/06/autonation-an-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2025 Q2","e":"an","d":"2025-07-25","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Bret Jordan","x":"Are you starting to see parts inflation passing through in the ticket?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/06/autonation-an-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2025 Q4","e":"an","d":"2026-02-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Mike Manley","x":"Also, sales in this year's fourth quarter were negatively impacted by the strong pull ahead earlier in the year as consumers reacted to the tariff announcements and purchased vehicles prior to the expiration of government incentives for electric-related powertrains.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/06/autonation-an-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2025 Q4","e":"an","d":"2026-02-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Mike Manley","x":"For example, when tariffs really became very much front of mind.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/06/autonation-an-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2025 Q4","e":"an","d":"2026-02-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mike Manley","x":"Adjusted earnings per share also excludes charges for severance expenses and asset impairments.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/06/autonation-an-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2026 Q1","e":"an","d":"2026-05-01","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Michael Manley","x":"As you'll remember, last year, there was a significant acceleration in demand following tariff-related announcements, which clearly set up a very challenging year-over-year comp.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/01/autonation-an-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2026 Q1","e":"an","d":"2026-05-01","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Thomas Szlosek","x":"Turning to Slide 5, I'll walk through our quarterly P&L. Total revenue for the quarter was $6.6 billion compared with $6.7 billion in the first quarter last year, which benefited from the tariff-related volumes, particularly in premium luxury to talk later.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/01/autonation-an-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2026 Q2","e":"an","d":"2026-07-31","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Michael Manley","x":"Now we're looking forward to the second half when the volume comparison headwinds from 2025 relating to tariff and EV credits lapse.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/07/autonation-an-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AN 2026 Q2","e":"an","d":"2026-07-31","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Michael Manley","x":"As expected, new unit sales were lower ver